## PR workflow

Every issue lands on `main` through a Pull Request. No direct commits to `main`.

<!-- IF:ADAPTER_CLAUDE -->| Step              | Skill              | What it does                                            |
| ----------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| 1. Pick an issue  | `/kit-task-sync`       | See the open board, choose what's unblocked             |
| 2. Start work     | `/kit-task-start <N>`  | Isolated worktree + branch `<kind>/<N>-<slug>` from the base + mark In Progress |
| 3. Do the work    | —                  | Code, write plans, etc.                                 |
| 4. Open PR        | `/kit-task-pr <N>`     | Commit + push + open PR with template/labels/milestone  |
| 5. Review + merge | `/kit-task-pr-merge`   | Squash-merge PR, switch to main, pull                   |
| 6. Close          | `/kit-task-close <N>`  | Close issue (auto on `Closes #N`) + archive plan        |
<!-- /IF:ADAPTER_CLAUDE --><!-- IF:ADAPTER_CODEX -->| Step              | Command                         | What it does                                            |
| ----------------- | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| 1. Pick an issue  | `cckit sync --llm`              | See the open board, choose what's unblocked             |
| 2. Start work     | `cckit start <N>`               | Isolated worktree + branch `<kind>/<N>-<slug>` from the base |
| 3. Do the work    | —                               | Work inside the worktree `cckit start` printed          |
| 4. Open PR        | `cckit pr <N> "<summary>"`      | Commit + push + open PR                                 |
| 5. Review + merge | —                               | A human decision; report the PR URL and stop            |
| 6. Close          | `cckit close <N> "<summary>"`   | Close the issue once its PR merged                      |
<!-- /IF:ADAPTER_CODEX -->

### Branch naming

`<kind>/<issue-number>-<slug>` — kinds: `task`, `plan`, `adr`, `scaffold`, `spike`.

### PR conventions

- Title = exact issue title · Body includes `Closes #N`
- Labels + milestone inherited from the issue · One PR per issue (coupled migration chains group into one) · Squash merge, linear history

